    "title": "pandas.Series.struct.explode — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.struct.explode#\n\n- Series.struct.explode()[source]#\n- Extract all child fields of a struct as a DataFrame. Each child field of the struct becomes a column in the resulting DataFrame, with column names matching the struct field names. \n  - Returns:\n    - pandas.DataFrame\n    - The data corresponding to all child fields.\n See also \n  - `Series.struct.field`\n  - Return a single child field as a Series.\n Examples >>> import pyarrow as pa >>> s = pd.Series( ... [ ... {\"version\": 1, \"project\": \"pandas\"}, ... {\"version\": 2, \"project\": \"pandas\"}, ... {\"version\": 1, \"project\": \"numpy\"}, ... ], ... dtype=pd.ArrowDtype( ... pa.struct([(\"version\", pa.int64()), (\"project\", pa.string())]) ... ), ... ) >>> s.struct.explode() version project 0 1 pandas 1 2 pandas 2 1 numpy",
    "markdown_length": 783,
